course: dictionary
lesson: 13134
title: Group words: footwear
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Footwear is a noun, which is a naming word. It is a group word, so it covers many different things at once. Shoes, boots, trainers and sandals are all footwear.
explain: Look at «The shop has a big footwear section on the top floor.» The word footwear tells you the shop sells shoes of many kinds, not just one sort. The context shows you that it is a group word.
explain: Schools use it in their rules too. «Please wear suitable footwear for science lessons.» Suitable means right for the job and safe, so you would wear trainers, not flip-flops or sandals with no backs.
fact: Footwear means things you wear on your feet.
fact: Footwear is a noun and has no plural: you say footwear, not footwears.
fact: Shoes, boots, trainers and sandals are all kinds of footwear.
fact: Footwear is a group word, like clothing, which covers many kinds of one thing.
exercise: «The shop sells footwear for children and adults.» What does footwear mean? | Things you wear on your head | Things you read in a book | Things you wear on your hands | *Things you wear on your feet
exercise: Which of these is footwear? | Gloves | *Trainers | Scarf | Hat
exercise: «Please wear suitable footwear for science lessons.» What does suitable mean here? | Made of paper | *Right for the job and safe | Too big to wear | Very expensive
test: «We need proper footwear for the hill walk.» Which word in this sentence is a group word for shoes and boots? | proper | hill | *footwear | walk
test: Which sentence uses footwear correctly? | The shop has footwears in the window. | I like the footwears. | The footwear are very fun. | *The shop has footwear for the whole family.
exam: Mia says, «Footwear is a group word.» Which sentence explains why she is right? | Footwear covers many kinds of shoes, such as boots, trainers and sandals | *Footwear is a group word because it covers many kinds of things worn on the feet | Footwear means something you eat | Footwear is a colour
